DHCP

Provides an IP address to every machine on the network and elminates configuration errors

Provided an IP from a scope ( A list of valid IP addresses available for assignment )


DORA:
Discover    -   Client asks for an IP to DHCP
Offer       -   Offers an IP within the scope
Request     -   If accepted, client requests for that IP
Acknowledge -   DHCP sends a lease containing which IP got taken and for how long

IP address
Subnet Mask
Default gateway IP
DNS server IP

DHCP Relay  -   Forwards DHCP packets between client and servers ( Typically only used when client and server are not located on same subnet / network )

Operates using UDP (fire and forget)

IP Helper   -   Forwards several different kinds of UDP broadcast across router and can be used in conjunction with the DHCP relay ( needed on clients router in order to have a properly working DHCP )